@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
title BASELINE c7338ad: delegation instructions and optional image helper
class "CLAUDE-codex-section.md" as instructions {
 codex exec read-only for code consultation
 foreground or background shell invocation
 workspace-write only when authorized
 image workflow references installed genimg.sh
}
class "genimg.sh" as helper {
 PROMPT strips all angle brackets [8-14]
 OUT made absolute [15-18]
 WORKDIR = mktemp -d [24]
 trap cleanup on EXIT [25]
 MODEL_ARGS and EFFORT whitelist [29-37]
 codex exec prompt on stdin [39-63]
 verify out.png [65]
 mkdir destination; mv out.png [66-68]
}
class "Temporary workdir" as temp {
 out.png
}
class "Codex CLI" as codex <<external>> {
 exec --sandbox workspace-write
 flags: skip-git-repo-check; ephemeral
 configured model or CODEX_MODEL
 CODEX_EFFORT default medium
}
class "Requested output path" as output <<user-owned>>
instructions --> helper : documented invocation
helper --> codex : prompt stdin in temporary cwd
codex --> temp : writes image (external behavior)
helper --> temp : validates output; cleanup
helper --> output : trusted script moves generated file
note bottom of helper
This diagram records existing Bash behavior.
No claim that angle stripping is a security boundary.
Image helper changes and macOS implementation are excluded
from Grok/Cline integration acceptance; no source changes planned.
end note
@enduml
